enchilada: MSS stage 9 (mss=9): WCN3990 copy engines, HTC, WMI, HTT and a passive scan (Wi-Fi round 5)

mss=9 = mss=8 plus the host side of the WLAN data path, after Linux v6.12 ath10k snoc.c, ce.c,
htc.c, htt_tx.c and wmi-tlv.c, ported from topaz 0123/0125. Stage 2 gives the WLAN stream (SID
0x40 mask 0x1, enchilada2.dtb icnss iommus) a free apps-SMMU SMR whose S2CR points at the bypass
bank CB(n-1) that 0193 sets up for USB, the way arm-smmu-qcom shares one bypass bank; it refuses
if that bank is not configured or the SID is already routed elsewhere. Once stage 8 reaches
mission mode: the twelve copy engines at membase 0x18800000 (+0x240000, RRI at +0x24c004,
shadow source write indices at +0x32000) with host_ce_config_wlan, 64-bit descriptors and the
read indices in DDR, polled; rings and buffers in 8 MiB of low DDR at 0xa1100000 that XNU does
not manage, mapped write-combined only. HTC READY, connect HTT_DATA and WMI_CONTROL (one credit,
use_fw_tx_credits = false; credit reports are 4-byte records, as htc.c parses them), then
SETUP_COMPLETE_EX; WMI-TLV SERVICE_READY -> INIT (ath10k_wmi_tlv_op_gen_init's resource config
and host memory chunks) -> READY; HTT VERSION_REQ, FRAG_DESC_BANK_CFG, RX_RING_CFG (htt_rx_desc_v2
offsets) and AGGR_CFG; a channel list with every channel passive, one station vdev and passive
scans every 15 s, logging each BSS once (SSID, BSSID, channel, RSSI). Nothing is transmitted.
Also fixes 0266: ath10k_hw_power_on comes before wlan_enable, so stage 8 now votes the WCN3990
supplies (mainline sdm845-oneplus-common &wifi: ldoa5 800, ldoa7 1800, ldoa17 1304, ldoa25 and
ldoa23 3300 mV, HPM) and RF_CLK2 through RPMh before wlan_cfg (new sweet_rpmh_wlan_power; votes
are never dropped). Any failure or timeout stops the WLAN path with a log line; wlan_mode off
and the 0262 stop path follow as before. mss<=7 behave as before.

